# Cloudflare Pages headers.
#
# The PRODUCTION build is a static export that talks only to the cable. It makes
# NO network requests of its own at runtime, which is what lets the policy below
# be this tight: connect-src is 'self' purely so the page can fetch its own assets.
#
# The PREVIEW is the one exception, decided by the operator on 2026-09-23 (docs/
# PLAN.md §8-1): owners holding `owner_preview` get per-owner SYNC — sessions they
# choose to send, and error records the app sends by itself — disclosed on m3's
# /preview-notice and in its privacy policy (#preview). Those requests go to
# /api/* on THIS origin, behind the owner gate (functions/), so 'self' already
# covers them and connect-src did not widen. Keep it that way: widening it to
# https: would give away the one property that makes a diagnostic tool safe to
# leave open in a garage.
#
# The same file serves both builds. The preview's responses also pass through
# functions/_middleware.ts, which keeps these headers and makes caching private.

/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data:; font-src 'self' data:; connect-src 'self'; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'none'; form-action 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: no-referrer
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  # Both hardware permissions are stated, and both are stated as (self).
  #
  # `usb=()` is an EMPTY allowlist, not a default: it makes
  # navigator.usb.requestDevice() throw SecurityError on the deployed origin.
  # That is the Android path — Chrome for Android exposes a navigator.serial
  # that enumerates only Bluetooth RFCOMM, so a USB K+DCAN cable is unreachable
  # there and has to be driven over WebUSB. With `usb=()` every Android session
  # would fail in a way indistinguishable from an OTG or cable fault on the
  # phone, which is the worst place to spend an afternoon.
  #
  # `serial` is listed even though omitting it currently permits it. Once
  # someone is editing this line, an unstated permission is one deletion away
  # from breaking desktop, and the deletion would look deliberate.
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), payment=(), usb=(self), serial=(self)
  # noindex on EVERYTHING, not only on the data.
  #
  # It used to be `/*.json` and `/ecu-data/*`, because those are the files with
  # a provenance question attached (THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md §3). But the pages
  # that LINK them are just as findable, and this whole deployment is meant to
  # sit behind a gate — a crawler reaching the index at all is a symptom worth
  # not having. It costs one header on assets nobody would index anyway.
  #
  # This is a REQUEST, not access control. The gate is what actually keeps the
  # tables private — the owner gate on the preview, Cloudflare Access on the
  # production project — and `noindex` and `robots.txt` only ask politely.
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex
